assistant: Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing in get_product
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 renamed the product's `price` field to `unit_amount`, even though the published OpenAPI spec didn't change. The value is still in dollars: the same product returns 1199 under both versions. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so it returned `price: null` for every v2 response. The fix adds an optional `unit_amount` field to the vendor product type and maps the price as `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. v1 responses still use `price` and give exactly the same output as before. typecheck, lint and test (including the repro) all pass. `search_products` only reads `price` too, so it will probably return no price for v2 search results. No v2 search traffic was recorded, and I left that file unchanged.

